    "body": "`Cython.Coverage` dropped only the line that matched an exclusion. coverage.py excludes the suite that line opens, so a `TYPE_CHECKING` import stayed missing in a `.pyx` report and was excluded in the same `.py` file.\n\n`exclude_also` is already part of `report:exclude_lines` before the plugin is configured. The plugin now also excludes the indented suite, using the source text so an `else` ends it even when that clause has no trace line. A comment does not end the suite. A match that does not open a suite, such as a pragma on an assignment, does not take the next line with it.\n\nThe source file has to be present for that scan. A suite that dedents inside parentheses is not recognized.\n\nBefore this change, `tests/run/coverage_exclude_block.srctree` left `import os` in `missing_lines` (`[7, 13]`) and excluded only the header. After it, that import is excluded, the `else` body is executed, and the pragma assignment does not exclude the following `return`. `tests/run/coverage_cmd.srctree` still reports pragma lines 17 and 19 missing and 18 and 20 excluded.\n\nOn this Windows locale, `runtests.py` fails while decoding MSVC's build output as UTF-8, including for the existing coverage command test. The same commands were run directly. Linux CI was not run here.\n\nCloses #8069.\n",
    "closed_at": null,
